  "findings": [
    "No duplicate full grayscale transform pass in ordinary eligible record-backed encoding: the first pass records coefficients and histograms; the second replays records after optimal tables exist. Tight/restart paths intentionally recompute. Do not remove a nonexistent ordinary second transform.",
    "WriteRecords22.18percent own samples follows each record through table family, symbol, Lengths and Codes arrays before separate Write/WritePair entry. Actual JIT confirms separate table/length/code loads and checks; sampled offsets are locations subject to skid, not isolated instruction costs.",
    "GrayRow230, CopyBlock149 and NormalizeRgba8123 samples locate another independent preparation lead; their total is not a measured standalone normalization phase. Existing eight-pixel GrayRow batching is already present.",
    "Current forward transform already uses exact AVX2 factorization/transposes; reciprocals prepare once per operation. No reason to replay prior transform/row arithmetic variants before addressing repeated record dispatch."
  ],
  "hypothesis": "Prepare one bounded packed Huffman symbol bank after optimal tables are built, then replay records using one family+symbol index and one code/length load. Investigate eliminating repeated table-object/array traversal and redundant writer pair dispatch without changing bits, per-record cancellation, MCU boundaries, stuffing/flushes or caller failure publication.",
  "intendedEndState": "One coherent prepared entropy replay boundary; no new general cache/session/pool or fixture specialization. A candidate1024entry uint bank needs4096stackbytes or explicitly admitted operation storage, charged within a justified substantial owner. Assess this against existing16KiB table allowance and actual overlapping table capacities before allocation. Temporary old/new representation must have a declared removal path; do not leave a test-only production writer alive.",
  "next": "First bound the bank layout and live table/record ownership, preserve or deliberately scope invalid arbitrary-table behavior using actual production call boundaries, then one main/embedded candidate perOS and existing completeRGBAgray short. Compression/exactness before timing; other encoder paths are affected if shared replay changes and require representative standalone costs at acceptance. No production change or prototype measurement yet.",
